Mumble is a Teamspeak-like confcall program and protocol that offers superior sound quality and bandwith utilization compared to for instance teamspeak. It's available for Mac OS, Linux and Windows, so every lojbanist should be able to join us :)

You'll need the [http://mumble.sf.net/|Mumble client], after the installation is finished, it will help you set up your audio settings for  maximum pleasure :)

jewel is kindly hosting a mumble server for us.

There's no need to register, just install mumble, type in the server address

subvert-the-dominant-paradigm.net

enter a username and the standard password: 'cakyrespa'.

Alternatively you can register and upload a picture for your account:

[http://subvert-the-dominant-paradigm.net/mumble-server/register.cgi]


